WEBVTT

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:04.780
Human blood.

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.410
Mr. Masaru!

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.260
Who is it?

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:31.140
-Narumi?
-Narumi!

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:40.700
We saw it. I'm sure we did.

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.620
Narumi's disappearing back.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:00.920
Before dawn, when the stars paint the sky

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:05.930
I am searching for the thing I lost

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:10.600
With a restless heart
Under the sun yet in the dark

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:15.230
I patch together little prayers
to light my path

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:19.980
I don't need anything,
as my hands are full

00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:24.780
My hands are full of emptiness

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:29.490
Please, just once, nod for me

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:34.370
Just once, reach out to me like the mirror

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:39.340
I will live for that single moment,
that single second

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:44.010
All the rest can just burn away

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:48.640
What's right for me is for me alone

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:53.890
Whatever the path, I'll follow it to you

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:58.360
This feeling grows and grows,
deep inside my heart

00:01:58.690 --> 00:02:01.940
For one single reason

00:02:02.110 --> 00:02:09.990
I continue to climb up on the stage

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:20.420
Narumi.

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:23.460
We have yet another new member in
the Nakamachi Circus.

00:02:23.630 --> 00:02:25.470
#9 Memories

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:27.470
His name is Guy.

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:30.720
We were helping
plane crash victims, when...

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:33.470
Shirogane, look.

00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:36.730
My teacher!

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:39.230
Teacher?

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:42.230
Are you okay...?

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:45.280
Éléonore.

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:57.460
Mr. Masaru.

00:02:58.210 --> 00:02:59.580
What is the matter?

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:06.550
That Guy, who is he to you?

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:09.720
Mr. Guy is my teacher.

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:11.600
-Teacher?
-Yes.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:18.730
My first living memory is
of traveling with Mr. Guy.

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:27.280
I was taken to a place in France
called Quiberon.

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:31.820
There, I was told to become
a puppet-handling puppet.

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:34.410
A puppet-handling puppet?

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:35.580
That's correct.

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:42.170
After much hard training, I lost
all emotions and became a real puppet.

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:48.720
But Mr. Guy was always there for me.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:51.260
I see. Sorry.

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:56.680
I just thought Narumi was the first person
who showed you kindness.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:01.440
I thought I saw Narumi
after the plane crash.

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:05.570
And I haven't been able
to get it off my mind.

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:07.400
Same with me.

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:13.200
Can you hear my heart beating?

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:18.830
Thump, thump.

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:23.380
Before, it used to go click, click.

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:25.590
Precise like a machine.

00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:30.170
But someone taught my heart
how to beat like a human's.

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:32.640
That someone was you.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:36.890
And now, my heart beats fast and strong.

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:40.560
It's because of the man
who still lives inside of you.

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:47.570
The first person to bring warmth
to my cold, frozen life...

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:53.910
You like Narumi, don't you?

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:00.870
I really like you too.

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:05.540
Thank you.

00:05:17.970 --> 00:05:19.100
It happened again.

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:22.140
He told me to live on strongly.

00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:25.230
He even died to save me, but I...

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:30.360
I'm so sorry.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:37.200
Shirogane is trying to overcome
her tough past.

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:41.410
But I'm not even trying to face mine.

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:47.460
Why did my father leave his entire fortune
to just me?

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:54.220
People are after my life for that,
and it got Narumi killed, too.

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:59.350
When you realize
that it's time to smile, don't cry.

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:08.060
I've made up my mind, Shirogane.

00:06:08.810 --> 00:06:11.820
I have to go find out why.

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:35.170
We were deep in the mountains of China
with only a small clue to guide us.

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:39.970
Our mission was to track down
the Midnight Circus

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:41.930
and destroy it.

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:45.100
This is Mingxia.

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:49.860
The daughter of Master Liang,
the man who taught me martial arts.

00:06:50.730 --> 00:06:53.820
We had gone to Master Liang's dojo
in search of clues.

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:56.740
There, we found out he'd contracted
ZONAPHA syndrome

00:06:56.900 --> 00:07:00.990
and left for his hometown
in search of a spring of immortality.

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:05.960
Lucille said if we found him,
we'd find the Midnight Circus.

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:09.500
Mingxia decided to come with us.

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:15.300
Master Liang's hometown is
where the "Bai" family...

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:21.720
My name is Francine.

00:07:27.140 --> 00:07:28.560
Is something wrong?

00:07:29.350 --> 00:07:30.440
I'm fine.

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:36.110
I've been having strange dreams.

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:42.370
According to Lucille, the Aqua Vitae
I was given was the last, thickest drop.

00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:46.750
The soul of the man who made
the Aqua Vitae was dissolved in it.

00:07:47.710 --> 00:07:51.750
So it seems like the dreams I'm having
are actually his memories.

00:07:59.260 --> 00:08:01.140
You came.

00:08:01.970 --> 00:08:03.390
-Master!
-Father!

00:08:05.510 --> 00:08:06.350
Father!

00:08:06.850 --> 00:08:08.350
Are you okay?

00:08:11.480 --> 00:08:12.900
What a riot.

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:16.360
You used to be so scary,
and now look at you.

00:08:16.530 --> 00:08:18.990
What's so funny? Watch your mouth!

00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:22.530
Thanks, I feel somewhat better.

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:28.330
The strange disease that can
only be eased by another's laughter...

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:30.710
ZONAPHA syndrome.

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:36.710
It is by divine retribution that I am
afflicted with this disease.

00:08:37.130 --> 00:08:38.510
What do you mean?

00:08:39.260 --> 00:08:43.430
My ancestor created a certain something.

00:08:43.590 --> 00:08:46.350
Something that should never
have been created.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:48.770
The water of life.

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:52.020
You mean, Aqua Vitae?

00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:56.570
And before I knew it,
I was telling him everything.

00:08:57.610 --> 00:09:01.320
That I had become a shirogane
by drinking the Aqua Vitae.

00:09:01.990 --> 00:09:04.870
And how I was now fighting the automata.

00:09:05.030 --> 00:09:08.540
That's enough!
You really think we'd fall for such a lie?

00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:11.040
She's right. There's no way he'd...

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:14.170
I see. You have been through a lot.

00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:17.340
Forgive me, Master.

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:20.510
I have talked too much about myself.

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:21.920
I do not mind.

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:29.140
Rather, if what you say is true,
there's something you must know.

00:09:32.690 --> 00:09:34.060
Listen carefully.

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:39.360
It all began over 200 years ago.

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:44.570
There were once two brothers in
the Bai family of puppeteers.

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:48.830
I know about this.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:54.710
The elder brother was Yin,
and the younger brother was Jin.

00:09:55.710 --> 00:09:59.550
I want to be able to make this puppet
move more like a human.

00:10:00.090 --> 00:10:01.760
Me too, Yin.

00:10:02.510 --> 00:10:06.760
No, it's the memory of the man
who is dissolved within me.

00:10:07.510 --> 00:10:11.810
The pair sought the answer in alchemy
and set out on a journey.

00:10:13.310 --> 00:10:18.810
After 8 years, they finally arrived
at the home of alchemy.

00:10:19.230 --> 00:10:21.400
Prague, the City of a Hundred Spires.

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:26.320
They became apprentices to
an old alchemist.

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:32.540
Look, it's Mr. Yin and Mr. Jin.

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:34.910
They're so handsome.

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:37.370
They come from faraway Qing.

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:39.960
No wonder they have such mysterious eyes.

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:43.670
Yin, those girls are watching us again.

00:10:43.840 --> 00:10:48.140
So? We have no time for women.

00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:53.930
Really? I think learning about women
may be another path to the Great Work.

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:56.350
Jin, leave me out of this.

00:10:56.640 --> 00:10:59.310
You still can't talk to women, huh?

00:10:59.650 --> 00:11:03.780
But the girls in town say
that they like that honesty about you.

00:11:03.940 --> 00:11:06.110
Stop teasing your big brother!

00:11:09.370 --> 00:11:10.240
Forgive me.

00:11:11.870 --> 00:11:13.950
You scared me.

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:24.300
You mustn't run out
into the street like that.

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:27.470
-Sorry.
-What's your name?

00:11:28.550 --> 00:11:31.930
My name is Francine.

00:11:32.430 --> 00:11:33.390
And you two?

00:11:34.180 --> 00:11:36.230
I'm Bai Yin.

00:11:36.390 --> 00:11:37.390
And I'm Bai Jin.

00:11:37.980 --> 00:11:40.060
Oh, you must be foreigners.

00:11:40.230 --> 00:11:43.230
What nice names. I like them.

00:11:46.110 --> 00:11:51.030
The two studied hard
and trained in alchemy.

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:52.490
They only had one goal.

00:11:53.410 --> 00:11:57.160
To use alchemy to breathe life
into puppets

00:11:57.330 --> 00:11:59.420
and make them move like humans.

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:02.420
Apples, apples. Tasty apples.

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:05.750
Nice and juicy. Oh!

00:12:06.590 --> 00:12:08.090
Yin, Jin!

00:12:09.550 --> 00:12:11.550
Can I go buy an apple?

00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:13.350
All right.

00:12:17.180 --> 00:12:19.390
Look, it's Francine again.

00:12:19.850 --> 00:12:21.730
Cozying up to Jin like that.

00:12:21.900 --> 00:12:22.980
That thief.

00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:27.570
Yin, there's a carnival today.

00:12:28.860 --> 00:12:31.030
Let's go. There will be jesters.

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:34.120
We have no time for that.

00:12:34.280 --> 00:12:35.950
Come on, just this once.

00:12:36.120 --> 00:12:38.950
-Besides, that girl...
-Let's go, Yin.

00:12:39.870 --> 00:12:43.040
I love jesters and entertainers.

00:12:43.540 --> 00:12:45.090
Come on.

00:12:59.810 --> 00:13:01.640
Here Francine, have some.

00:13:02.480 --> 00:13:03.690
Thanks.

00:13:08.280 --> 00:13:09.360
She's saving them?

00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:11.740
What next?

00:13:11.900 --> 00:13:13.740
I want to see the puppet show.

00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:16.870
Bro, puppets.

00:13:17.660 --> 00:13:18.490
What?

00:13:18.660 --> 00:13:21.580
We're from a family of puppeteers.

00:13:24.370 --> 00:13:25.330
Huh?

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:27.800
Aren't you putting on the show?

00:13:27.960 --> 00:13:32.260
Can't. The puppeteer is too drunk
to do the play.

00:13:32.420 --> 00:13:34.680
That's too bad.

00:13:34.840 --> 00:13:36.100
Let's go, then.

00:13:37.100 --> 00:13:41.480
Sir, you're in luck,
these two are puppeteers.

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:42.480
Hey!

00:13:42.640 --> 00:13:45.850
Now's your chance to make money.
Why not let them do it?

00:13:46.270 --> 00:13:48.110
Hey, we didn't say we would.

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:54.740
I'm sorry. I just wanted to
see you two doing puppets.

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:56.740
Come on, why not?

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:00.700
Okay, fine.

00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:07.500
Jeez, look at that smile on her face.

00:14:18.140 --> 00:14:19.180
Hey, Jin.

00:14:19.560 --> 00:14:22.470
He's had one too many Pilsner beers.

00:14:23.430 --> 00:14:25.890
He's happy because the crowd loved it.

00:14:27.190 --> 00:14:30.400
We're not here to put on a show.

00:14:30.730 --> 00:14:33.570
But you got all this bread in return.

00:14:33.780 --> 00:14:36.860
Moldy bread? Keep it if you want.

00:14:37.030 --> 00:14:39.160
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:42.540
-Then...
-Take it all.

00:14:44.620 --> 00:14:45.710
Thank you.

00:14:48.790 --> 00:14:50.290
Bye then.

00:14:50.750 --> 00:14:52.000
I'll take you home.

00:14:52.170 --> 00:14:54.050
-You don't have to.
-Let me.

00:15:02.640 --> 00:15:05.480
I didn't know Prague had such backstreets.

00:15:06.310 --> 00:15:08.150
Every city has them.

00:15:08.440 --> 00:15:11.570
There are always more poor people
than rich people.

00:15:12.980 --> 00:15:14.530
I'm home.

00:15:14.690 --> 00:15:15.990
Sis's back!

00:15:16.490 --> 00:15:17.650
You're home!

00:15:17.820 --> 00:15:20.030
Look what I brought you today.

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:21.950
Snacks and bread.

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:24.540
So that's why.

00:15:24.700 --> 00:15:26.460
This man gave them to me.

00:15:26.870 --> 00:15:28.500
Say thank you everyone.

00:15:28.790 --> 00:15:30.210
Thank you!

00:15:31.250 --> 00:15:32.710
R-Right.

00:15:33.210 --> 00:15:36.260
-Smells so good.
-I haven't had bread for so long.

00:15:36.420 --> 00:15:39.720
I thought you'd sold your hair again.

00:15:40.430 --> 00:15:43.970
Oh, shush. Not in front of the bread.
Be happy.

00:15:44.430 --> 00:15:47.980
Besides, I think I look good
with short hair.

00:15:48.640 --> 00:15:51.860
I'll be going out for a while, so eat up.

00:15:52.110 --> 00:15:54.520
Yin, make yourself at home.

00:15:55.610 --> 00:15:56.740
Where is she going?

00:16:08.710 --> 00:16:09.620
Hey!

00:16:12.170 --> 00:16:14.840
The mark of a thief!

00:16:15.500 --> 00:16:17.050
You know now.

00:16:17.260 --> 00:16:19.220
That I'm a bad person.

00:16:20.010 --> 00:16:22.010
Why did you steal?

00:16:24.390 --> 00:16:25.560
Oh dear.

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:29.390
You haven't eaten?
But you had bread with you when you left.

00:16:29.560 --> 00:16:31.770
I... I shared it.

00:16:31.940 --> 00:16:34.980
Don't give your food away to strangers.
Come on.

00:16:35.150 --> 00:16:36.610
Where are we going?

00:16:36.780 --> 00:16:39.320
To get your bread back.

00:16:50.410 --> 00:16:54.380
See? I can go a day without bread.

00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:56.130
I'm going home now.

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:58.300
Hey.

00:16:58.460 --> 00:16:59.420
Who's there?

00:17:00.510 --> 00:17:02.260
Our Lady Francine.

00:17:02.430 --> 00:17:03.680
Our Lady?

00:17:03.840 --> 00:17:05.680
Oh? Who are you?

00:17:06.310 --> 00:17:08.430
I'm a friend of hers.

00:17:08.600 --> 00:17:11.270
Oh, of Her Ladyship's?

00:17:11.600 --> 00:17:12.810
Her Ladyship?

00:17:13.400 --> 00:17:16.110
Could you tell me more about her?

00:17:16.440 --> 00:17:18.860
She's an angel.

00:17:19.780 --> 00:17:24.820
She escaped from a French slave trader
and settled here in Prague.

00:17:24.990 --> 00:17:27.990
She does odd jobs and sells her hair.

00:17:28.160 --> 00:17:33.330
She uses the money to care for
orphans and us poor people.

00:17:35.210 --> 00:17:37.590
I heard she stole something.

00:17:39.960 --> 00:17:44.090
One single egg it was.

00:17:45.430 --> 00:17:48.890
A lonely orphan caught pneumonia.

00:17:49.060 --> 00:17:51.640
She wanted to give the child nutrition.

00:17:52.850 --> 00:17:53.810
But...

00:17:56.440 --> 00:18:00.150
the egg never made it to the child.

00:18:00.320 --> 00:18:04.530
Another poor man had ratted her out
for a measly reward.

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:13.830
The child died, and she was locked up
for a month.

00:18:15.370 --> 00:18:18.630
You are her lover, are you not?

00:18:19.210 --> 00:18:20.750
No, I'm just...

00:18:21.090 --> 00:18:25.380
I beg you, make her happy.

00:18:25.840 --> 00:18:29.350
She is our angel, our saint.

00:18:30.680 --> 00:18:34.600
Starting that day,
Yin began to think differently.

00:18:38.190 --> 00:18:39.730
What's wrong, Yin?

00:18:40.690 --> 00:18:43.610
You're not focused at all these days.

00:18:47.660 --> 00:18:51.910
Alchemy is a discipline that
allows one to seek the truth.

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:54.660
The knowledge helps nobody but ourselves.

00:18:54.910 --> 00:18:57.290
Yeah, of course.

00:18:57.870 --> 00:19:03.090
Jin, what light is there in a path
that is not paved for another?

00:19:04.510 --> 00:19:08.840
I have come to think like that
because of a certain event.

00:19:09.260 --> 00:19:10.300
An event?

00:19:11.510 --> 00:19:14.100
You don't mean Francine, do you?

00:19:16.020 --> 00:19:20.400
Wait a minute, what happened
the night I got drunk?

00:19:20.690 --> 00:19:23.940
Nothing, that's not what I meant.

00:19:24.440 --> 00:19:29.610
Yin, you know I fell in love
with Francine first.

00:19:29.870 --> 00:19:32.530
You can't take her from me.

00:19:32.780 --> 00:19:33.990
No freaking way.

00:19:34.790 --> 00:19:36.000
Yin!

00:19:41.040 --> 00:19:44.300
Jin hasn't talked to me since.

00:19:58.890 --> 00:20:00.270
Francine.

00:20:00.730 --> 00:20:03.730
Oh, Yin. Thank you for the other day.

00:20:04.900 --> 00:20:06.230
What were you praying for?

00:20:09.070 --> 00:20:11.160
It's a bit embarrassing.

00:20:13.120 --> 00:20:17.290
I was hoping all illnesses
would disappear from the world.

00:20:18.830 --> 00:20:24.090
She thinks only of others,
even though she's in distress herself.

00:20:25.170 --> 00:20:27.630
How deep and wide her heart is.

00:20:28.630 --> 00:20:29.800
What is it?

00:20:30.630 --> 00:20:34.010
If it's with this woman... I could...

00:20:38.770 --> 00:20:42.940
Francine, will you be mine?

00:20:52.610 --> 00:20:54.320
But I was a thief.

00:20:54.820 --> 00:20:56.330
It means nothing to me.

00:20:56.990 --> 00:20:59.700
I can't leave those children.

00:21:00.160 --> 00:21:03.250
I'll get a job and feed everyone.

00:21:04.130 --> 00:21:05.710
But your alchemy...

00:21:06.250 --> 00:21:08.210
I care for it no longer.

00:21:09.260 --> 00:21:10.470
Francine, I beg you.

00:21:12.130 --> 00:21:14.140
Marry me.

00:21:25.020 --> 00:21:29.070
This is all I have now,
but I'll buy you a better ring someday.

00:21:30.240 --> 00:21:31.900
No, I like this one.

00:21:42.460 --> 00:21:44.920
What's this?

00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:47.170
I'm crying.

00:22:14.530 --> 00:22:16.910
Fly up high, Marionette

00:22:17.070 --> 00:22:19.240
Turn to ash, gracefully

00:22:19.410 --> 00:22:23.710
My only purpose in life was to fight

00:22:23.910 --> 00:22:28.460
Why am I so angry
even I dump my humanity

00:22:28.630 --> 00:22:34.840
Without you, I can't smile anymore

00:22:35.880 --> 00:22:40.060
I assume that I am to be blamed

00:22:40.220 --> 00:22:44.350
Like a puppet that can't smile naturally

00:22:44.770 --> 00:22:49.730
I feel like someone is pulling my strings

00:22:49.900 --> 00:22:53.440
What am I even living for?

00:22:53.610 --> 00:22:57.780
I was hurt, and thought
that nobody would understand

00:22:57.950 --> 00:23:02.910
But you came along,
and took me in your arms

00:23:03.080 --> 00:23:08.790
I felt my tangled arms and legs

00:23:09.330 --> 00:23:11.420
become free

00:23:11.590 --> 00:23:14.130
Fly up high, Marionette

00:23:14.300 --> 00:23:16.340
I think now I can reach you

00:23:16.510 --> 00:23:20.850
Before I met you, I was empty

00:23:21.010 --> 00:23:25.730
Now I have something
I'd give my all to protect

00:23:25.890 --> 00:23:32.150
You taught me how to feel,
the feeling of sorrow too
